WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:03.334
Welcome, welcome, welcome
to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:03.334 --> 00:00:05.067
You're here!
You're watching. You made it.

00:00:05.067 --> 00:00:06.868
Thank you for being here.

00:00:06.868 --> 00:00:08.567
Well, guys, as the country

00:00:08.567 --> 00:00:10.334
continues to deal
with the pandemic,

00:00:10.334 --> 00:00:13.067
the director of the CDC
just said that she's aiming

00:00:13.067 --> 00:00:16.100
to improve the agency's
COVID messaging.

00:00:16.100 --> 00:00:17.701
Yeah, then
in her next interview,

00:00:17.701 --> 00:00:21.033
she said the CDC is not aiming
to improve their messaging.

00:00:21.033 --> 00:00:23.267
[ Laughter ]

00:00:23.267 --> 00:00:25.801
Yeah, in the CDC's defense,
it's hard to get any message out

00:00:25.801 --> 00:00:30.033
when every ad on TV
is for Caesars Sportsbook.

00:00:30.033 --> 00:00:32.567
Yep, the CDC wants
to communicate more clearly,

00:00:32.567 --> 00:00:34.667
so going forward,
their press releases

00:00:34.667 --> 00:00:36.901
will no longer be
in the Wingdings font.

00:00:42.567 --> 00:00:45.200
Some more news.
I read that Neil Gorsuch

00:00:45.200 --> 00:00:47.067
is the only
Supreme Court justice

00:00:47.067 --> 00:00:50.067
who won't wear a mask
to help protect his colleague,

00:00:50.067 --> 00:00:52.734
Sonia Sotomayor,
who has diabetes.

00:00:52.734 --> 00:00:55.601
[ Audience boos ]

00:00:55.601 --> 00:00:57.100
You know Gorsuch is the guy

00:00:57.100 --> 00:00:59.067
who touches every bagel
before picking one.

00:00:59.067 --> 00:01:01.801
You know that? He's like...

00:01:01.801 --> 00:01:04.100
You guys remember Neil Gorsuch.

00:01:04.100 --> 00:01:07.000
He used to work
for the law firm

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:09.033
Rogan, Hogan &amp; Facebook.

00:01:09.033 --> 00:01:11.467
Hey, I saw a news anchor
in Mexico who looked like

00:01:11.467 --> 00:01:13.200
he finally hit
his breaking point

00:01:13.200 --> 00:01:14.901
with people
who won't get vaccinated.

00:01:14.901 --> 00:01:16.133
Check this out.

00:01:16.133 --> 00:01:18.501
-iUstedes! [Bleep]

00:01:18.501 --> 00:01:22.167
[ Shouting Spanish ]

00:01:22.167 --> 00:01:24.234
[Bleep]

00:01:24.234 --> 00:01:26.100
[ Shouting Spanish ]

00:01:26.100 --> 00:01:27.667
[Bleep]

00:01:27.667 --> 00:01:29.634
[ Shouting Spanish ]

00:01:37.934 --> 00:01:40.334
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:40.334 --> 00:01:42.300
[ Laughter ]

00:01:42.300 --> 00:01:44.567
♪♪

00:01:44.567 --> 00:01:46.300
-Yo!

00:01:46.300 --> 00:01:49.534
You know that's how Dr. Fauci
feels on the inside.

00:01:49.534 --> 00:01:51.901
[ Laughter ]

00:01:51.901 --> 00:01:54.701
Hey, I heard that today
former New York City mayor

00:01:54.701 --> 00:01:56.834
Bill de Blasio announced
that he is not running

00:01:56.834 --> 00:01:59.501
for Governor of New York.
He then --

00:01:59.501 --> 00:02:01.934
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:01.934 --> 00:02:04.667
[ Laughter ]

00:02:04.667 --> 00:02:07.801
He then waited over ten minutes
for someone to say, "Aw."

00:02:07.801 --> 00:02:09.167
[ Laughter ]

00:02:09.167 --> 00:02:10.901
Yep, de Blasio
won't run for governor.

00:02:10.901 --> 00:02:12.834
He said he wants
to spend more time at home

00:02:12.834 --> 00:02:16.067
being booed by his family.

00:02:16.067 --> 00:02:17.367
Did he really
have to announce that?

00:02:17.367 --> 00:02:19.267
I mean, he might as well
have announced that he won't be

00:02:19.267 --> 00:02:21.200
performing at the Super Bowl
Halftime Show.

00:02:21.200 --> 00:02:22.667
It's like, "Yeah, we know."

00:02:22.667 --> 00:02:24.868
Some business news here.
Apparently airlines

00:02:24.868 --> 00:02:27.033
are dealing with
the ongoing pilot shortage

00:02:27.033 --> 00:02:30.868
by raising pay
and lowering the requirements.

00:02:30.868 --> 00:02:32.400
[ Laughter ]

00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:35.501
Passengers said, "That's nice."
And, "Wait. What?"

00:02:35.501 --> 00:02:37.467
[ Laughter ]

00:02:37.467 --> 00:02:39.200
This probably explains
why my last pilot

00:02:39.200 --> 00:02:40.801
was wearing a Petsmart uniform.

00:02:40.801 --> 00:02:42.734
[ Laughter ]

00:02:42.734 --> 00:02:45.501
Yeah, it's not very reassuring
when your pilot is the same guy

00:02:45.501 --> 00:02:47.534
who drove your Uber
to the airport.

00:02:47.534 --> 00:02:49.801
He's like, "Alright. Let's go.
Here we go. Come on."

00:02:49.801 --> 00:02:52.534
[ Laughter ]

00:02:52.534 --> 00:02:55.133
Now instead of needing
years of experience, pilots just

00:02:55.133 --> 00:02:58.634
have to complete a CAPTCHA
that proves that they're human.

00:02:58.634 --> 00:03:00.501
Yeah, they'll hire anyone
right now.

00:03:00.501 --> 00:03:02.834
Here's the newest United pilot
I saw.

00:03:02.834 --> 00:03:07.634
-[ Shouting Spanish ]

00:03:07.634 --> 00:03:09.968
[ Applause ]

00:03:09.968 --> 00:03:13.133
-That's a bit much.
-Geez.

00:03:13.133 --> 00:03:16.200
-Well, speaking of flying,
a man went viral on TikTok

00:03:16.200 --> 00:03:19.167
when he shared his experience
as the only passenger

00:03:19.167 --> 00:03:22.434
on an eight-hour
international flight.

00:03:22.434 --> 00:03:24.701
Somehow we have a pilot
and passenger shortage.

00:03:24.701 --> 00:03:26.133
I don't know.

00:03:26.133 --> 00:03:29.234
Of course, they wouldn't let him
board until his zone was called.

00:03:31.133 --> 00:03:32.901
"Group two."

00:03:34.901 --> 00:03:37.100
"Sorry, sir.

00:03:37.100 --> 00:03:40.634
You're group four.

00:03:40.634 --> 00:03:43.834
Group two. One more time."

00:03:43.834 --> 00:03:45.834
It's weird
when the pilot's like,

00:03:45.834 --> 00:03:49.100
"Uh, we will now be making
our approach, Tom."

00:03:49.100 --> 00:03:50.934
Hey, this is also going viral.

00:03:50.934 --> 00:03:53.133
Someone posted a video
of a FedEx driver

00:03:53.133 --> 00:03:56.100
who didn't exactly deliver
their package with care.

00:03:56.100 --> 00:03:57.634
Watch this.

00:03:57.634 --> 00:04:00.934
-Woman in audience:
Oh, no.

00:04:00.934 --> 00:04:03.934
[ Laughter ]

00:04:08.100 --> 00:04:10.601
His boss called him and said,
"Just a little more practice,

00:04:10.601 --> 00:04:14.701
and you can do it without
slowing down the truck."

00:04:14.701 --> 00:04:16.200
Respect for that aim,
though, huh?

00:04:16.200 --> 00:04:17.734
-Yeah, that was good aim, man.

00:04:17.734 --> 00:04:20.434
-Finally, a woman in Canada
was driving on a frozen river

00:04:20.434 --> 00:04:23.300
when the ice broke
and her car started to sink.

00:04:23.300 --> 00:04:26.567
And instead of panicking,
she took a selfie.

00:04:26.567 --> 00:04:27.968
Take a look.

00:04:30.200 --> 00:04:32.901
Don't worry. When the river
saw that it was a yellow Subaru,

00:04:32.901 --> 00:04:34.968
it spit the car right back up.

